# Q4 2025 Revenue Report ~title

## Executive Summary ~summary

Revenue grew 23% year-over-year, driven primarily by enterprise
expansion. Our [cloud platform]{~highlight} continues to be the
primary growth driver. ~p-intro

![Revenue chart](revenue-q4.png) ~chart1

## Key Metrics ~metrics-heading

| Metric       | Q3 2025 | Q4 2025 | Change |
|--------------|---------|---------|--------|
| ARR          | $42M    | $51M    | +21%   |
| Net Revenue  | $12.5M  | $15.4M  | +23%   |
| Customers    | 340     | 412     | +21%   |
| NRR          | 118%    | 122%    | +4pp   |
~metrics-table

The {{c1}}enterprise segment{{/c1}} showed the strongest growth,
contributing 67% of new ARR. ~p-enterprise

Mid-market expansion was [ahead of plan]{~highlight} by 12%,
driven by the new self-serve onboarding flow.

> We're seeing unprecedented demand in the mid-market segment.
> The pipeline for Q1 is already 40% larger than this time last year.
> -- Sarah Chen, VP Sales
~pull-quote

## Regional Breakdown ~regional-heading

![Regional map](regions.png) ~region-map

- North America: +28% YoY
- EMEA: +19% YoY
- APAC: +31% YoY (fastest growing)
~region-list

***

## Outlook

We expect continued growth through H1 2026, with particular
strength in healthcare and financial services verticals.

Key {{c2}}risks include macro headwinds{{/c2}} in European markets
and potential currency effects on APAC revenue.

{{pagebreak}}

## Appendix ~appendix

Detailed breakdown by vertical available in the supplementary data.

![Vertical breakdown](verticals.png) ~vertical-chart

